from pathlib import Path
import csv,statistics as st,collections,re
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
d={v:[{r['case']:float(r['ns']) for r in csv.DictReader(open(p/f'helper-confirm-{v}-{i}.csv'))} for i in range(5)] for v in ['base','head']}
lines=['# Performance by helper family','','PR e8ea6fced00 versus matching main 00236714c28; Cortex-X925. This analysis combines the original 456-case direct-helper screening with new longer runs of 21 representative cases.','','## Longer representative checks','','Five alternating process launches per side, 150 ms per case per launch; same runtime and CoreLib, only JIT changed. Custom Stopwatch harness, not BenchmarkDotNet. Table reports median time change; negative means faster. All nonzero integer count/search gains below have non-overlapping observed ranges, including the 4.3% result.','','Integer inputs, match in the last lane:','','| Helper | Vector64<int> | Vector128<int> |','|---|---:|---:|']
ops=['Count','IndexOf','LastIndexOf','Any','All','None','CountWhereAllBitsSet','IndexOfWhereAllBitsSet','LastIndexOfWhereAllBitsSet']
for op in ops:
 vals=[]
 for width in [64,128]:
  n=f'V{width}_int_{op}_last';b=st.median(r[n] for r in d['base']);h=st.median(r[n] for r in d['head']);vals.append(f'{100*(h/b-1):+.1f}%')
 lines.append('| '+op+' | '+' | '.join(vals)+' |')
lines+=['','Additional controls: Vector128 long/float/double Count with the same match placement were unchanged. Gains depend on element type and lowering path.','','## Full initial screening','','Screening rule: more than 5% median change and no overlap among five process samples. These are screening flags, not statistical significance claims.','','| Helper | Cases | Faster | Initially slower |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
g=collections.defaultdict(list)
for r in csv.DictReader(open(p/'comparison.csv')):
 if r['case'].startswith('V'):g[r['case'].split('_')[2]].append(r)
for op in ops:
 rs=g[op];fast=sum(float(r['change_pct']) < -5 and r['ranges_separate']=='True' for r in rs);slow=sum(float(r['change_pct']) >5 and r['ranges_separate']=='True' for r in rs);lines.append(f'| {op} | {len(rs)} | {fast} | {slow} |')
lines+=['','The one initial slower Count/NaN flag disappeared in the previous longer confirmation. Any/None benchmark instruction sequences were identical on both sides; All was identical except four constant-NaN cases with minor register/loop changes and no measured gain.','','## Assembly evidence','','Vector128<int> LastIndexOf wrapper grew from 136 to 144 bytes while its longer-run time improved by 10.9%. Its lowering replaces mask extraction, transfer to a general register, and leading-zero count with a vector select and horizontal minimum before extracting the result. This demonstrates that a larger sequence can run faster for this case. Wrapper sizes include the measurement loop.','','Count uses a shorter vector shift/horizontal-add sequence instead of mask extraction and population count.','','## Limits and attribution','','These measurements distinguish which API calls improved when switching the entire PR JIT on and off. They do not isolate interactions between individual implementation changes; that would require JIT builds with each helper family enabled separately.','','The unchanged dotnet/performance span benchmarks remain a different workload: 23 of 24 unchanged at the 5% threshold and a length-4 Span<int>.LastIndexOfValue regression confirmed at 5.8%. A faster direct LastIndexOf helper does not guarantee every inlined span caller improves.','','The harness does not cover every supported element type, every input, or other ARM64 CPUs. Any/All/NoneWhereAllBitsSet are not measured by these direct cases. No recommendation to remove those imports follows from these results alone.','','Reproduce representative runs with `python3 helper-confirm.py`; source generator: `generate.py`; raw files: `helper-confirm-{base,head}-{0..4}.csv`. Disassembly: `base-disasm.txt` and `head-disasm.txt`.']
(p/'HELPER-BREAKDOWN.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
